    {
     "ord": 3,
     "period": {
      "start": "1939-09-26",
      "end": null
     },
     "periodStartPrecision": "day",
     "periodEndPrecision": null,
     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "華沙投降與地下組織",
      "en": "Surrender of Warsaw and the underground"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "美國陸軍戰史載，9月26日晚，波軍使者攜羅梅爾的信越過德軍防線，請求停火二十四小時並談判投降。次日庫特爾茲巴將軍代表羅梅爾接受德方條件，戰事於9月27日14時停止。IPN 的文章寫道，9月26日托卡熱夫斯基-卡拉舍維奇將軍向羅梅爾提出組織地下抵抗的構想；羅梅爾最終同意，並簽署了任命。9月27日成立的勝利服務波蘭（SZP）由該將軍出任司令。",
      "en": "The US Army history records that on the evening of 26 September Polish envoys crossed the German lines with a letter from Rommel asking for a 24-hour ceasefire and a surrender parley. The next morning Gen. Kutrzeba accepted the German terms in Rommel's name, and hostilities ceased at 1400 on 27 September. An IPN article says that on 26 September Gen. Tokarzewski-Karaszewicz put his underground plan to Rómmel, who finally agreed and signed the appointment. The SZP, founded on 27 September, was commanded by that general."
     },
